  <main>
    <section class="intro section-shell"><p class="eyebrow">NOTES / EVIDENCE</p><h1>What changed because something went wrong.</h1><p class="lede">Short records of the checks, failures, and operating habits behind the projects.</p><button class="intro-scroll-cue" type="button" aria-label="Scroll to next section"></button></section>
    <section class="section-shell"><div class="note-grid"><article class="note-card"><span>01 · DEBUGGING</span><h3>Diagnose from evidence</h3><p>Compare independent clients, logs, effective configuration, and runtime behavior before changing the system.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>02 · OPERATIONS</span><h3>Test recovery</h3><p>A service that starts is not enough. Reboots, failed power, backups, and restores need direct verification.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>03 · PUBLICATION</span><h3>Explain without exposing</h3><p>Share architecture, reasoning, and results while keeping addresses, credentials, serials, and private infrastructure private.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>04 · NETWORKING</span><h3>Test the boundary</h3><p>When a connection fails, compare routes, ARP, firewalls, applications, and devices before blaming the server.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>05 · SECURITY</span><h3>Preserve the controls</h3><p>Keep Secure Boot, key-based SSH, private access, encrypted backups, and least exposure in the design.</p></article><article class="note-card"><span>06 · MEASUREMENT</span><h3>Make claims testable</h3><p>Use health checks, metrics, load tests, outage tests, and restore tests to turn “it works” into evidence.</p></article></div></section>
    <section class="section-shell"><div class="feature-card"><div class="card-kicker">READ THE CASE STUDY</div><h3>These notes belong to real projects.</h3><p>Flashpoint supplies the application problems. The Home Server supplies the operating environment. The notes record what each system taught us.</p><div class="card-footer"><a class="text-link" href="/projects/">Browse projects →</a><a class="text-link" href="/home-server/">Read the home-server story →</a></div></div></section>
